{"id": "1211.4000", "lane": "market_microstructure", "ledger": "1614-performance-of-betting-lines-predicting-nfl-games.md", "note": "2,560 NFL games 2002-2011; LD mean -0.009, sd 13.588; Pr(F>U|P=p)=Phi(p/13.588) calibrated (p=7: 0.697 vs 0.689); >2,000/2,560 games moved <=1 point; abstract claims 53.5% home-underdog ATS but Table 1 shows 409-396 (50.8%) - flagged as internal inconsistency.", "title": "The Performance of Betting Lines for Predicting the Outcome of NFL Games", "type": "paper", "verdict": "ADAPT"}
{"id": "1811.12516", "lane": "market_microstructure", "ledger": "1615-fair-odds-for-noisy-probabilities.md", "note": "Noisy-probability equilibrium theory of favorite-longshot bias: fair odds must exceed 1/P_C when P_C>0.5 and fall below when P_C<0.5; at w1=1/2, eps=1, P_T->1/2 seller margin = ln(1-w1)/w1+1 = -0.39; buyer bets when 1/P_C>2, seller when 1/P_C<2. Adapt as ensemble-dispersion wedge adjustment.", "title": "Fair Odds for Noisy Probabilities", "type": "paper", "verdict": "ADAPT"}
{"id": "2607.17991", "lane": "market_microstructure", "ledger": "1616-optimal-market-making-in-prediction-markets.md", "note": "First stochastic-control market-making framework for binary prediction markets; logit-belief diffusion with sigma(t,x)=sigma0+sigma1(t/T)^eta+sigma2/(1+x^2); 10,000-path Monte Carlo optimal vs myopic: mean PnL 12.39 vs 12.47, std 10.34 vs 28.11, VaR5% 4.20 vs 32.41, ES5% 9.68 vs 40.50.", "title": "Optimal Market Making in Prediction Markets", "type": "paper", "verdict": "ADAPT"}
{"id": "2605.09599", "lane": "market_microstructure", "ledger": "1617-adaptive-liquidity-in-prediction-markets-via-online-learning.md", "note": "Adaptive liquidity via log-sum-exp mixture C^mix=(1/beta)log(sum w(k)e^{beta C_k}); Hessian = expected expert curvature + beta*Cov(expert gradients); worst-case loss overhead only (1/beta)log M; hybrid signal Gamma=a(centered slippage)+b(liability); O(sqrt(T log T)) switching regret; code released.", "title": "Adaptive Liquidity in Prediction Markets via Online Learning", "type": "paper", "verdict": "ADAPT"}
{"id": "2608.00666", "lane": "market_microstructure", "ledger": "1618-executable-arbitrage-and-market-efficiency-in-prediction-markets.md", "note": "Payoff-space vs protocol-executable no-arbitrage; 32,702 events, 259M trades; $1.118M mechanism-linked profit: $1.086M converter-enabled (97%), $32,283 settlement-based; CLOB 2,098 positive YES-side vs 36 NO-side violation episodes; median durations 16.15s vs 7.99s; median profit/conversion decayed $1.00->$0.20->$0.08.", "title": "Executable Arbitrage and Market Efficiency in Prediction Markets", "type": "paper", "verdict": "ADAPT"}
{"id": "2603.26620", "lane": "market_microstructure", "ledger": "1619-optimal-parlay-wagering-and-whitrow-asymptotics.md", "note": "Exact parlay Kelly = outer product of one-event strategies (x_gamma^*=prod c_ell^* prod s_{ell,i_ell}^*); active-ticket criterion (no inactive leg in optimal parlay); Whitrow asymptotics x_j^sim=(1-Lambda_j eps^2)x_j^ind+O(eps^4); forbidding parlays costs only O(eps^4) growth - quantitative backbone of GSE singles stance; binary check f1=m1(1-m2^2)/(1-m1^2 m2^2).", "title": "Optimal Parlay Wagering and Whitrow Asymptotics: A State-Price and Implicit-Cash Treatment", "type": "paper", "verdict": "ADAPT"}
